<title>USA: University of South Ala., yields 4.70 pct in 2002.</title>
<headline>University of South Ala., yields 4.70 pct in 2002.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thorton Farish, Inc said it priced $7.055 million of University of South Alabama, tuition revenue refunding bonds, Series 1996-B, with a top yield of 4.70 percent in 2002.</p>
</text>
